                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Actually you need a neutral review button for this game. \nCrysis 2 didn’t age well. \nI played the game back in 2011 on ps3 and pc. I know how it felt to see those graphics. I mean crisis back then was the fps game. \nIf you look at this game now many mechanics are out of date. \nThe enemies made me rage. Some enemies are bullet sponges, most of the enemies suffer from I’m being hit but stumbling and stumbling and refusing to die. The AI makes the enemies behave in a strange way. Sometimes they flank you sometimes the ai resets and there run around like mindless chickens. The aliens storm you and stumble through you and you think they are dead but they aren’t and then they kill you from behind. It is a very strange behaviour. \nThe weapon variety is just laughable. You have like 10 weapons to chose from. \nThe amount of ammo you get is laughable too. Mostly you need 40 rounds to kill an enemy and then you have to search for crates \nThe most rage raising thing was the sprint which drains your energy. Sometimes you get flanked by enemies then you energy is already half way through and then you pop armour suit and try to flee in order to take cover but then you are out of energy and instead of sprinting you jog to your next cover. This was a reason for many cheap deaths. \nUnfortunately the graphics are not a pretty as I remember them. Back in 2011 crisis was awesome now it’s just dumb. Crisis is still video game history.",
